---
import source from '../../../demo/basic/main.l?raw';
import version from '../../.generated/version.json';
import { Code } from '@astrojs/starlight/components';
import RustPipeline from './RustPipeline.astro';
const paths = [
  { n: '01', title: 'Learn L', text: 'Start with a real program. Follow values, names and paragraphs through to Apps and Services.', link: '/docs/guide/', action: 'Follow the guide', icon: 'book' },
  { n: '02', title: 'Know the language', text: 'Read the specification, exact grammar and supported behavior—with the boundaries made explicit.', link: '/docs/spec/', action: 'Read the specification', icon: 'code' },
  { n: '03', title: 'Build locally', text: 'Install the compiler from source, build for your native host and keep companion artifacts together.', link: '/docs/cli/', action: 'Use the CLI', icon: 'compiler' },
];
---
<div class="l-home">
  <section class="l-hero" aria-labelledby="home-heading">
    <div class="l-hero-copy">
      <p class="l-eyebrow">The L programming language</p>
      <h1 id="home-heading">Readable source.<br /><span>Applications<br class="l-break" /> as values.</span></h1>
      <p class="l-intro">Describe programs in sentences. Build Apps, organize their code with Services, and coordinate App execution. L generates Rust source and builds it into native programs you can run.</p>
      <div class="l-actions"><a class="l-primary" href="/docs/guide/first-program/">Start with Hello World <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a class="l-secondary" href="/docs/spec/">Explore the language</a></div>
      <p class="l-status"><span class="l-status-channel"><span class="l-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span> {version.languageVersion ?? 'Unreleased'} / {version.channel === 'production' ? 'Release' : 'Local'}</span><span>English source lexicon</span><span>macOS &amp; Linux</span></p>
    </div>
    <div class="l-example">
      <div class="l-example-label"><span>FROM THE REPOSITORY</span><a href="/docs/guide/first-program/">demo/basic/main.l ↗</a></div>
      <Code code={source} lang="l" title="Hello World" />
      <div class="l-output"><span>EXPECTED STDOUT · EXISTING TEST WITNESS</span><pre>Hello World!{ '\n' }</pre></div>
      <p class="l-example-note">Source included at build time. This website build does not execute L examples.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <div class="l-principles" aria-label="Language overview">
    <div><strong>Sentences with structure</strong><span>Names, phrases and explicit meaning.</span></div>
    <div><strong>Applications as values</strong><span>Build, run, await and inspect.</span></div>
    <div><strong>Native output</strong><span>Generated Rust. Native executables.</span></div>
  </div>
  <section class="l-start" aria-labelledby="start-heading">
    <div class="l-section-heading"><div><p class="l-eyebrow">A place to begin</p><h2 id="start-heading">Read it. Build it. Run it.</h2></div><p>From the first sentence to the process model, follow one concept at a time.</p></div>
    <div class="l-paths">{paths.map((p) => <a href={p.link} class="l-path"><div class="l-path-top"><span class="l-icon" style={`--l-icon: url(/assets/l/icons/${p.icon}.svg)`} aria-hidden="true"></span><span>{p.n}</span></div><h3>{p.title}</h3><p>{p.text}</p><strong>{p.action} <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></strong></a>)}</div>
  </section>
  <section class="l-build" aria-labelledby="build-heading">
    <div><p class="l-eyebrow">A compiler, then a program</p><h2 id="build-heading">Build once.<br />Run the result.</h2><p>The build command produces a native executable and any required companion programs. Building does not execute your program.</p><a class="l-text-link" href="/docs/cli/installation/">Source installation and prerequisites →</a></div>
    <div><Code code={'bash ./install.sh\n./bin/l build ./demo/basic/main.l\n./demo/basic/main'} lang="sh" title="From the repository root" /><p class="l-small">Follow the <a href="/docs/cli/installation/">source-install prerequisites</a>. Keep the executable and its <code>.apps</code> directory together.</p></div>
  </section>
  <section aria-labelledby="pipeline-heading" class="l-pipeline">
    <p class="l-eyebrow">From source to execution</p><h2 id="pipeline-heading">From L source to native programs</h2>
    <p>L generates Rust source, then uses the Rust toolchain to build native programs for your macOS or Linux host. Run the resulting executable to start your program.</p>
    <RustPipeline />
    <div class="l-reference-links"><a href="/docs/internals/architecture/">Compiler architecture →</a><a href="/docs/reference/logemes/">Logemes and AML →</a><a href="/docs/stdlib/">Standard-library dictionaries →</a></div>
  </section>
</div>
